## CORE RULES

**NO MOCKS, NO SHORTCUTS, NO HACKS**
- All implementations must be production-ready
- Complete features fully or not at all
- No temporary solutions, workarounds, or "quick fixes"
- No simplified versions, hardcoded values, or debug-only code
- No TODO placeholders that become permanent

**DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT**
- If Feature A needs Feature B, stop A and complete B first
- All dependencies must be fully implemented before proceeding
- No partial implementations allowed
- Maintain clean dependency hierarchy

**ERROR HANDLING**
- All error conditions must return proper errors
- Code must be deterministic and predictable
- No silent failures or undefined behavior
- Fallbacks require explicit approval and must have a real reason to exist
- Return errors when conditions are not satisfied

**TESTING**
- All tests must use real implementations (no mocks)
- Complete coverage including edge cases
- Integration tests required
- No test-only code in production builds

## PROHIBITED

❌ Mock implementations
❌ Placeholder functions
❌ Hardcoded test values
❌ "We'll fix it later" approach
❌ Skipping proper error handling
❌ Implementing features in isolation
❌ Simplified implementations
❌ fallbacks without explicit aproval an solid justification


